      "subject": "fix(ui): prevent chat empty-state text overlap (#89)",
      "body": "* fix(ui): prevent textarea caret from bleeding into centered heading\n\nThe 'What do you want to create?' heading in the empty chat state\nshares a vertically-centered absolute wrapper with the textarea\ninput below it. The textarea's blinking caret was visually bleeding\nthrough the heading text because both occupied the same stacking\ncontext with no explicit z-index separation.\n\nAdd position: relative + z-index: 1 to .centeredHeading so it paints\nabove the textarea's caret layer. The heading already unmounts when\nthe bar docks on first send, so this only affects the empty state.\n\n* fix(ui): push empty-state text above the centered input to prevent visual collision\n\nThe empty-state content (icon + 'Ready for the next build.') uses\nheight: 100% + justify-content: center, centering it in the message\narea. The InputBarShell heading ('What do you want to create?') and\ninput pill are also vertically centered via absolute positioning.\nBoth occupy the same panel center, causing the empty-state text to\nvisually crowd into the heading.\n\nAdd padding-bottom: 45% to .emptyState so it settles into the upper\nthird of the panel, reading as a lead-in above the centered input\nrather than colliding with it.",
